  "slug": "trees-phylogenetic-d93f",
  "summary": "Quantum annealing, million-taxon coalescent inference, and exact rooted-tree partitioning now make tree-level problems tractable at larger scales.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is reformulating core phylogenetic tree tasks as computationally tractable problems, although the items differ substantially in methodology. QUANTA recasts weighted quartet bipartitioning as a QUBO problem solved by quantum annealing on D-Wave hardware for species tree estimation. QRAFT targets scalability within a statistically consistent coalescent framework, with near-linear time and linear memory for million-taxon inference. PhytClust exactly optimizes monophyletic partitioning of rooted trees without a threshold and selects the number of partitions automatically. HYphlow addresses workflow integration, connecting taxon reconciliation, trait-based foreground assignment, and HyPhy selection analyses in an open-source Python GUI. What is new is the pairing of exact or statistically consistent formulations with new hardware and scale targets, rather than a shared algorithm.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-09"
}
